 "teaching": {
  "synthetic": true,
  "point": "An accessory pathway lets ventricular muscle start depolarising before the AV node has finished delaying. The PR shortens and the QRS begins with a slow, muscle-to-muscle upstroke: the delta wave. The Tier-3 model assumes the AV node is the only route, so its timing is wrong here by construction.",
